+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates input against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. Invalid input returns a `ToolResponse` describing the failed constraint, and the executor is not invoked. ([validated by rejects missing required input and passes valid extra properties through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11))
+
+Validation reports the failing property path and expected type without including the offending input value. ([validated by rejects a wrong-typed field without leaking its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L35))
+
+A static tool schema is compiled once at registration, while a function-valued definition is resolved and validated against on every call. ([validated by compiles static schemas once and uses the current function-valued schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L52))
+
+An uncompilable static schema fails during registration and names the tool. ([validated by rejects an uncompilable schema at registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L91))
